    "updated_at": "2022-09-09T23:01:16Z",
    "body": "To be clear, there are actually two invariants that all browsers are violating in this scenario, and which I'd really like preserve:\r\n\r\n- `go(n)` followed by `go(m)` ends up like `go(n + m)`\r\n- Traversals must never create a state which the user has never seen before. They must instead traverse to some already-seen state.\r\n\r\n#6315 does guarantee these, so we know it's possible!",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
